<title>USA: U.S. HomeCare says lawsuit settled.</title>
<headline>U.S. HomeCare says lawsuit settled.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. HomeCare Corp said Thursday it has settled litigation related to its 1992 acquisition of the assets and home infusion business of Home Infusion Pharmacy Services Inc and Able Health Management Services Inc.</p>
<p>Terms of the settlement were not disclosed. But the company said it was within its established reserves.</p>
<p>U.S. HomeCare spokesman Gerald Boisvert said the litigation was initiated by principals of the two acquired companies and involved a dispute over the purchase price. U.S. HomeCare had filed counterclaims.</p>
</text>
